{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474517-children-of-gaia-tribebooks","id":1474517,"title":"Children of Gaia tribebooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-12T14:31:20-08:00","id":1474517,"title":"Children of Gaia tribebooks","content":"I am reading and reviewing (in Spanish) all the tribebooks in my channel. And when I have arrived to the CoG (the 8th on the list) I have found a very mixed reaction from the fandom. This is a tribe that, in some way, is a paragon of the game, with the Fianna, probably the tribe most representative of the themes and lore of Werewolf the Apocalypse. It is a tribe deeply loved by lot of fans, also, and played by the power and utility of the gifts. But, on the opposite, I have found many people who dislike this tribe and, specially, the tribebook. They see them as bland, uninteresting and excessively positively depicted in a game about monsters. What do you think about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T15:00:08-08:00","id":1474521,"title":"","content":"I think for a lot of North American fans (and plenty of European ones that share a similar issue) the CoG represent the Garou in the worst possible way. They're the Tribe of the White Savior Complex. They're upper middle class activists that don't want to put their privilege at risk, so end up with a lot more talking than doing. They're too centrist to be the bomb throwing radicals of the punk side of the game, and too lefty to function well within the class conflicts of WtA as presented.<br /> <br /> To me, they're one of the easiest Tribes to remove because all they really do is eat up space other Tribes (mostly Older Brother, the Bone Gnawers, and Glass Walkers) should be occupying to make room for them. There's nothing they add to the game that you need their perspective to really highlight instead of just being a Camp or cross-Tribal Camp.<br /> <br /> The Revise Tribebook is one long series of this. All the attempts to make them like like they're doing subversive things, or pushing boundaries, or having a niche of their own, just fall flat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T17:33:57-08:00","id":1474536,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem, even 30 years ago, was the constant attempt to present the Children of Gaia as essentially &quot;Hippy&quot; hold overs and pacifists, based almost entirely on a late 19th and mid 20th century utopian mindset. The problem is that not only does this not apply all that well with characters outside the &quot;Western&quot; world, it also conflicts badly with the entire concept of Garou being Gaia's Fangs and the duties that entails. And the revised tribe book sort of doubled down on this.<br /> <br /> My preferred take has always been that they view violence and bloodshed as being a tragic necessity in their world, but that they prefer to use it as a method of last resort. They'd much prefer to try to save a Fomori by exorcising the Bane inside it and healing it rather than killing it, but sometimes that isn't possible, and death is the most merciful course of action. <br /> They also understand that it's the natural Garou behavior to challenge each other for dominance, but believe that fighting among themselves is a waste of time and resources which could be better spent on confronting the Wyrm (and Weaver). This is especially true of any inter-werewolf conflict which results in the death of a Garou. Non-violent challenges are therefor the preferred method of solving disputes. <br /> I also place them as one of the three tribes of leadership within the Garou nation. (The others are the Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords, as well as the fallen Croatan.) In their own way, many of them are every bit as bossy and power hungry as those other two tribes, but this tends to manifest in the &quot;Elite Savior Complex&quot;, but also paternalistic behavior, passive aggressive social bullying, and more than a little self-righteousness. <br /> If I were to try to sum the tribe up in a single word/theme, it would be Unity. The unification of the Garou Nation as a whole (under their enlightened leadership, naturally), unification and harmony of the material and spiritual aspects of both themselves and of the world, the mindsets of human and wolf, humanity with Gaia, and the various polarities/frequencies of gender, race, religion, sexuality, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T03:43:39-08:00","id":1474558,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback. I also have the perspective of the Children of Gaia as one of the tribes of leadership, with the arrogance and complex of superiority associated with their moral ground. One of the most attractive things to me it is the lack of a human culture behind, as a reference. Children of Gaia could be branded as hippies, and even as the western new-age guys, but they share a philosophy that was present from Paris to San Francisco.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T08:45:45-08:00","id":1474566,"title":"","content":"Their original human cultural influence/kinfolk breeding stock was, IIRC, supposed to be Southwest Asia, running from parts of modern day India to the Middle East, especially in the very early Bronze Age civilizations in the Indus River Valley and between the Tigris and Euphrates Rivers. There's apparently some Indus civilization imagery that's sometimes described as early &quot;unicorns&quot;, but which are clearly more derived from cattle than from horses, which ties in with their tribal totem, as well as offering a possible connection with the lost Apis were-aurochs.<br /> <br /> This would, naturally, evolve into later Vedic, Persian, Babylonian, Hebrew and perhaps Phoenician cultures, and eventually Hellenistic, possibly fully entering Europe and becoming part of its Garou population during the Roman period. So during the Roman Empire, the Children of Gaia may be tied to a lot of the &quot;Eastern Mystery Cults&quot; that were popular during the time. This would include the Christians who eventually dominated, but also a lot of the various fertility religions (Cybele, Isis, Bacchus/Dionysus, etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 02-13-2022, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T09:22:48-08:00","id":1474569,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem with the Children of Gaia is that they never quite developed from the original stereotype they were meant to fill. Other tribes got much more detailed over time and their stereotypes were lessened. Children of Gaia? Still remain mostly a white middle-class hippy in stereotype.<br /> <br /> It isn't helped by the fact that not even the WRITERS wanted to touch the tribe much. As such, we get Children of Gaia revised while other tribes get much better books.<br /> <br /> The best way to treat the Children of Gaia, in my opinion, is a tribe that kills people with kindness. They turn aggression to shame and fights into childish behaviour. They manipulate and direct the Nation through their guilt-tripping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T10:38:58-08:00","id":1474573,"title":"","content":"I've ditched the hippy aspect completely and run with the quiet unity angle instead. Coggies in my game are numerous, patient, insightful, and just as political as anyone else. They don't try to compete when it comes to grandstanding, but instead work on individuals, seek to empower them, nurture them, and show the value of working together instead of dominating and fighting each other. In essence, they point out the weaknesses of every other tribe's approach, and then present themselves as the mature, Gaia-oriented alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T11:24:21-08:00","id":1474575,"title":"","content":"From my experience, people who dislike the CoG tribebooks do so from two perspectives. The first group are people who don't like the general description of the tribe. The tribebooks are just more of that. The second group are people who do like the general description of the tribe, but feel the tribebooks did not do a good job of presenting/detailing what they liked about it.<br /> <br /> In fact, I think both groups probably agree on what it is they don't like. I think the major issue is that the supposed theme of the tribe - peace - conflicts with both the description of the Garou and their struggle against the Wyrm, and the setting itself (the game is about being savage warriors, not social workers engaged in conflict resolution). It makes the tribe look stupid, weak, and useless. Players don't know how to reconcile this tension between the two so the tribe appears incoherent. And the stereotype of the passive aggressive stoned hippie who preaches and moralizes to the others smacks of smug superiority that just annoys people.<br /> <br /> I believe the solution is to go back to the actual description of unicorn is actual myth and legend - unicorns are fierce, untamed animals that protect purity and innocence, whether that is unspoiled wilderness, small children, or something else. That reconciles the CoG holding peace to be important (to protect those who would be inadvertently harmed during conflict) while also being martial (because they are the protectors). If that doesn't work for you, well, everyone's mileage and tastes are different.<br /> <br /> Many years ago I explored some of that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn\">in this post</a>. I am including the link in case anyone gets use out of it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T11:51:49-08:00","id":1474577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474517-children-of-gaia-tribebooks?p=1474566#post1474566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their original human cultural influence/kinfolk breeding stock was, IIRC, supposed to be Southwest Asia, running from parts of modern day India to the Middle East, especially in the very early Bronze Age civilizations in the Indus River Valley and between the Tigris and Euphrates Rivers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was something added later once it was obvious that they needed some sort of history to them. The early books painted them much like the Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers that didn't have any strong ties to a specific ethnicity.<br /> <br /> But even 1e core book uses hippies to describe them (even if it is meant to be superficially so).<br /> <br /> A big problem is that the Children of Gaia have no way their early ethnic origins can really be played into the Tribal culture. Older Brother is accepting of all indigenous and oppressed peoples in contrast to Younger Brother's staunch Native American/First Nations only policy. The Silver Fangs, Glass Walkers, and Bone Gnawers all shed their origins on some level to embrace the local variations of socio-economic power. The Black Furies and Silent Striders have weaker connections to their original ethnicities for reasons, but haven't abandoned them completely.<br /> <br /> Attempts to make the whole Fertile Crescent origin for the CoGs work wasn't horrible, but it doesn't really fit well enough to ever come up.<br /> <br /> If you really wanted them to work with that background (it would be a bit cringy for the Middle East Tribe, but since when has that stopped the WoD?), the CoG should be the Tribe of Lawyers, not pacifists. They would be the overworked public defender to the Silver Fang's powerful DA's office and the Shadow Lord/Glass Walker functionaries of influence. Their history in the birth place of Hammurabi's Code, and the reactionary theology of early Judaism, meeting up with the Greek legal philosophers, going into the Islamic Golden Age, etc. There's an extremely clear cut history they could be part of that uses the law as a tool to better society instead of empower the wealthy; with failures aplenty, just look at old Draco's reputation. It makes their mediator focused principles way easier to divorce from White Savior mentality (not that it can't also be a critique of that, see Too Kill a Mockingbird). There have always been humans that have said, &quot;what if we could just make the law better so society would be better?&quot; and that really should be the core of the CoG approach.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T13:16:39-08:00","id":1474580,"title":"","content":"Alright, thanks for your insight. It seems that many people found the same problems in the CoG. On the other hand, many people also think that CoG are the first reference when thinking about Werewolf the Apcalypse. They are the monster ecologists who try to save the world, serve Gaia and protect the humanity.<br /> <br /> This is a bit of-topic. But some of you said that the CoG were the representation of the old hippie movement and the upper-middle white class thinking. Do you think that this message could be applied to the game as a whole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T14:11:00-08:00","id":1474584,"title":"","content":"I like the Children of Gaia, but I also see several flaws in their presentations:<br /> They have exclusive access to a self-healing Gift and are one of the few tribes with Luna's Armor. As of revised, they have a Gift for excessive amounts of damage on Adren, too. And they have a gift that allows them to simply be faster than any pursuer. It is, as if the authors just didn't know when to stop, if they added something pacifist/healing oriented, they felt the need to counter act that with another Gift, making the combination ridiculous in the process.<br /> <br /> Also, a lot of the moderated views of the tribe are just normal human standard and therefore the baseline for any lost cub homid. Hell, even back in 1st Edition, iirc, there were septs banning certain challenges because of the loss of garou live. Like Klaive duelling being something, hotheaded Fostern did in at dawn, because the Elders of any tribe wouldn't approve if it wasn't something like duelling for the leadership of a Silverfang house like Arkady and Albrecht did.<br /> <br /> Then there was this more esoteric goal to make Gaia whole again, returning everything to a Dawn Times state, which was even more far fetched as reaching the True Gaia Realm was for Stargazers. On the other hand there was stuff like the &quot;orgies&quot; splinter cell, with their special &quot;Breaking the Litany&quot;-Rite, and then again super militant members of the tribe. With a lot of tribes, the authors tried to force a niche for any archtype in a given tribe, but with the Children of Gaia, one often feels like they overdid it. Oh, and their own stick-fighting rules, because that is something that the WoD desperately needed, more nuances and options in the combat system, as if the WoD games were combat oriented in a way d20 games are, and not, at their core, storytelling games.<br /> <br /> 1st Edition wasn't well rounded in many ways, but simply talking to the Elders and explaining them what their tribe was all about should not be a sufficient Rite of Passage, yet it was the framing story of the Tribebook, iirc.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I like their &quot;fight the Wyrm where it breeds means in the hearts of the humans&quot;-approach. Their tendency to heal/redeem/repair makes for great stories when an NPC fails or an PC succeeds, just to proof hardliners wrong. Then again, you can't do that too often, or it looses it's impact and drama.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T14:20:18-08:00","id":1474585,"title":"","content":"Not just WtA, but even the whole original WoD. The whole classic games, in hindsight at least, feel painfully obvious in their white middle class left-political stance. The early creators for the games where people for whom the plights of the many people far more disadvantaged than they were resonated. So they wanted to write games that highlighted the social ills they saw. But that outsider perspective plagues the games to a fundamental core.<br /> <br /> None of it was malicious. A lot of them got well deserved credit for bringing up topics most games completely ignored. The problems set in as time passed, as being a white allies helping mainstream minority problems turned into not really listening to minority voices about how they were being represented in the games; let alone finding ways to give minority voices actually creative platforms in the games.<br /> <br /> Which the CoG reflect in an ironic sort of way: the come in, see problems, and want to fix those problems on their terms, rather than finding out what the people there actually want as a solution.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T14:40:05-08:00","id":1474586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474517-children-of-gaia-tribebooks?p=1474585#post1474585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which the CoG reflect in an ironic sort of way: the come in, see problems, and want to fix those problems on their terms, rather than finding out what the people there actually want as a solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they?<br /> I mean, some might. There are certainly CoGs who would act this way, but there are certainly other CoGs who are more empathic/experienced/educated than that, especially since CoG aren't necessarily tied to one ethnicity but can very well have members from each minority that isn't inherently tied to another tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T15:35:03-08:00","id":1474588,"title":"","content":"Yes. Remember that the CoG primary focus is other Garou. They want to be the mediators that ensure conflicts within the Nation don't come down to violence and bloodshed. They can't have members in the other Tribes to act as cultural ambassadors. When a Fenrir and one of Younger Brother get into a fight, the CoG want them to settle it their way. They see the centuries of animosity between the two Tribes as a danger that hatred (the Wyrm) will override the situation. So they want to get in the way, ensure peaceful discussions of what happened, and constructive actions moving forward. Meanwhile both Garou would have long since rather been left to get into a simple dominance fight, determine a winner, and move on.<br /> <br /> The CoG's secondary efforts with humanity suffer from the impact of the same mentality. Even with cultural ambassadors by being a diverse Tribe, with diverse kin as well, they're Garou, with Rage and The Curse. The Bone Gnawers are particularly unkind towards how little the CoG understand who the individuals among humanity are instead of what humanity's problems on a macro scale are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T22:36:54-08:00","id":1474600,"title":"","content":"Well, okay, I see how this approach is problematic. I don't necessarily see, that this something members of the CoG would necessarily do as their default approach to this extent, but it is certainly with the way I understood their depictions.<br /> <br /> Although, for all it flaws, I like one particular idea from the revised TB. It is about how the CoG blame themselves for the War of Rage's duration and cruelty, stating that they could broker negotiations with the fera, but whenever they tried to bring other local garou to the table to come to a mutual agreement, it ended in disaster and often bloodshed. It took them a long time to communicate within the tribe, that the world wasn't ready (yet) for their kind of harmony and co-operation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T02:37:28-08:00","id":1475440,"title":"","content":"I recently have finished reading the revised tribebook. It had some flaws and some good ideas. But I understand why many people does not like it, the level 3 ritual that allowed to redeem a Black spiral and clean their corruption is as interesting as it breaks the good vs evil conception of many people about werewolf; The ritual that allows you to control your rage having sex in crinos is just bizarre; Some characters embrace the hippy stereotypes, as the theurge premade character, and others seem only defined by being gay or part of a minority. I do not know how many times the authors remembers us that Ringer is gay and how proud is about it.<br /> <br /> However, the book had some good ideas, I liked linking the gaia with the persian and sumerian cultures, I liked the gifts and the fetishes and I liked the most the two end pages about how to use peace as a theme for a chronicle, opposing the blind militarism that usually impregns Werewolf, planting the seed of some moral dilemmas in the game.<br /> <br /> In conclusion, in my opinion, it is not a brilliant book, but neither one of the worst. I think that could be improved and better, but the idea of the tribe is still workable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T06:10:50-08:00","id":1475449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474517-children-of-gaia-tribebooks?p=1475440#post1475440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In conclusion, in my opinion, it is not a brilliant book, but neither one of the worst. I think that could be improved and better, but the idea of the tribe is still workable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem comes when it is compared to how other tribes were developed in their own tribebooks in <i>Revised</i>.<br /> <br /> Basically, the problem with the book is that it fully embraces the <i>stereotype</i> of the tribe instead of deepening things, and does so through the simplest storytelling paths available. So you either hates the tribe because you hate the stereotype and the book confirms your bias, or you like the tribe because you picture them beyond the stereotype and the book falls short of your expectations.<br /> <br /> No one really likes the <i>Stereotyped</i> CoG (although a couple <i>characters</i> like that wouldn't be a problem), because it is one of the most obtuse stereotypes in WtA, and if taken at face value it undermines the setting's premises for no pay-off at all (instead of bringing all the allusions we like when we like the tribe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}